        <title>Special Marine Warning issued June 3 at 12:34PM EDT until June 3 at 1:00PM EDT by NWS Key West FL</title>
        <summary>SMWKEY

The National Weather Service in Key West has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Hawk Channel and Straits of Florida from Craig Key to west end of
Seven Mile Bridge out 20 nm...
Bayside and Gulf side from Craig Key to west end of Seven Mile
Bridge...

* Until 100 PM EDT.

* At 1233 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located over Sombrero Key
Light, moving east at 5 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly higher
waves, frequent lightning, and heavy downpours.

* Locations in the warning include...
Sombrero Key Light, East Turtle Shoal Light, and East Washerwoman
Shoal Light.</summary>
